  concept: "Authored objective: Diagnose and recover all three sensor-chain faults.\nAuthored
    requirement: Recorded from the electrical graph, valid calibrated feedback and
    the level\u2019s verified run history.\nGeneral teaching principle: Sensor outputs
    require proper calibration, reference and freshness before they can support a
    diagnosis.\nOnly fresh, authoritative game evidence can establish that this objective
    is complete."
  analogy: A measuring ruler is useful only if zero and units are correctly established.
  diagram: '[Authored setup] -> [Check prerequisites] -> [Observe the game evidence]
    -> [Verify objective]'
  misconception: An old, uncalibrated or missing sensor reading is not reliable evidence.
